Chapter: MahjongWasm
  cites Games chapter Mahjong
  cites Foreword chapter List

 The browser interface for Mahjong Solitaire, on the handle contract in
 games-backlog.md GAME-11. A hundred and forty-four tiles are past an i32,
 so the page holds the state's address.

 `remove-pair` writes both slots through `list-set-at`, which mutates in
 place, so `mj-wasm-step` copies the tile list first.

 The layout holds thirty-six tile types, four of each. A tile's TYPE is
 what matches, not its value, which is why `mj-wasm-type` is exported: a
 page must not work out that a type is the value minus one over four.

 We say:

Section: Copying

  mj-copy-tiles : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  mj-copy-tiles (src) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 144 then acc
    else mj-copy-tiles src (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at src i))

  mj-copy-state : MahjongState -> MahjongState
  mj-copy-state (st) =
    MahjongState {
      tiles = mj-copy-tiles (st.tiles) 0 [],
      removed = st.removed,
      matched = st.matched,
      remaining = st.remaining
    }

Section: The Browser Interface

  mj-wasm-new : Integer -> MahjongState
  mj-wasm-new (seed) = mahjong-new seed

  mj-wasm-tile : MahjongState, Integer -> Integer
  mj-wasm-tile (st) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= 144 then (-1)
    else list-at (st.tiles) i

  mj-wasm-type : Integer -> Integer
  mj-wasm-type (v) = if v <= 0 then (-1) else tile-type v

  mj-wasm-free : MahjongState, Integer -> Integer
  mj-wasm-free (st) (i) =
    if i < 0 then 0
    else if i >= 144 then 0
    else if tile-present st i == False then 0
    else if tile-free st i then 1 else 0

  mj-wasm-removed : MahjongState -> Integer
  mj-wasm-removed (st) = st.removed

  mj-wasm-matched : MahjongState -> Integer
  mj-wasm-matched (st) = st.matched

  mj-wasm-remaining : MahjongState -> Integer
  mj-wasm-remaining (st) = st.remaining

  mj-wasm-stuck : MahjongState -> Integer
  mj-wasm-stuck (st) = if mahjong-stuck st then 1 else 0

  mj-wasm-pair : MahjongState -> Integer
  mj-wasm-pair (st) = find-matching-free-pairs st

  mj-wasm-step : MahjongState -> MahjongState
  mj-wasm-step (st) =
    if st.remaining <= 0 then st
    else let code = find-matching-free-pairs st
    in if code < 0 then st
    else remove-pair (mj-copy-state st) (code / 144) (rng-mod code 144)

  mj-wasm-done : MahjongState -> Integer
  mj-wasm-done (st) =
    if st.remaining <= 0 then 1
    else if mahjong-stuck st then 1
    else 0

Section: Playing By Hand

 `mj-wasm-step` finds a pair AND takes it, so a person cannot choose which
 pair goes. These take the two tiles the player picked instead, and they
 check the choice rather than trusting it: both tiles present, both FREE,
 both the same type, and not the same tile twice.

 Free is the whole rule of this game and it is not a property of the tile,
 it is a property of where the tile is sitting: `tile-free` asks whether
 anything is on top of it or hemmed in beside it. A page that only checked
 the types would let a player take a matched pair out of the middle of the
 pile, which is the game's one real constraint gone.

  mj-wasm-can-take : MahjongState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mj-wasm-can-take (st) (i) (j) =
    if i < 0 then 0
    else if j < 0 then 0
    else if i >= 144 then 0
    else if j >= 144 then 0
    else if i == j then 0
    else if tile-present st i == False then 0
    else if tile-present st j == False then 0
    else if tile-free st i == False then 0
    else if tile-free st j == False then 0
    else if tile-type (list-at (st.tiles) i) /= tile-type (list-at (st.tiles) j) then 0
    else 1

  mj-wasm-take : MahjongState, Integer, Integer -> MahjongState
  mj-wasm-take (st) (i) (j) =
    if mj-wasm-can-take st i j == 0 then st
    else remove-pair (mj-copy-state st) i j

 The two halves of the hint, so the page can point at a pair rather than
 take it. The code is `i * 144 + j`, which is what `find-matching-free-pairs`
 answers and what `mj-wasm-step` reads.

  mj-wasm-pair-a : Integer -> Integer
  mj-wasm-pair-a (code) = if code < 0 then (-1) else code / 144

  mj-wasm-pair-b : Integer -> Integer
  mj-wasm-pair-b (code) = if code < 0 then (-1) else rng-mod code 144

